<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African retail sales fall marginally in January.</title>
<headline>S.African retail sales fall marginally in January.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African retail trade sales fell a seasonally adjusted 0.03 percent month-on-month in January to 11.43 billion rand, latest Central Statistical Service (CSS) data shows.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, seasonally adjusted retail sales were up 9.9 percent from 10.41 billion rand in January 1996, the CSS said.</p>
<p>On an actual basis, retail trade sales were down 40.5 percent month-on-month and up 9.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Retail trade sales at current prices.</p>
<p>(rand million):</p>
<p>				 Jan '97	 Dec '96	Jan '95</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted  11,434.1	11,438.0     10,406.0</p>
<p>    Actual		   10,144.7	17,060.4	9,268.4</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
